  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "V1-A01",
      "description": "All furniture sizes, materials, people, lighting and positions are proposed, not surveyed. Original ERP geometry and assumptions remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A02",
      "description": "Far end means the east end of Jeu principal, x1710–1920. The house has a115cm raised play deck,252cm overall height and no bed. Stairs/slide, guarding and headroom require specialist design before fabrication; displayed children are scale figures."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A03",
      "description": "Dual-purpose transverse counter:60cm low registration hatch and102cm coffee cabinet, both55cm deep; one operator behind with85cm floor aisle in the retained211.5cm-high alcove. Water, drainage, power and equipment remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A04",
      "description": "Downstairs positions and counter retained from1.1.0. Upstairs now models30children and30seatedparents plus3staff, independently sized; an occupancy study, not a verified capacity certificate."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A05",
      "description": "Playhouse retained; upper deck remains visual only. Furnishings and shown people have collision proxies; routes are reserved and actual movement is tested. Downstairs queue/GTLE boarding operation unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A06",
      "description": "Queue study uses60x60cm waiting cells and a90cm local passage/entrance-turn target. Five adults fit tightly in two short files; the sixth intrudes into the entrance turning target. No stroller, luggage, whole-family or regulatory capacity allowance."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A07",
      "description": "Coffee plan/overview temporarily clips the existing facade and hides the alcove ceiling for a cutaway. Those original surfaces return in first person and other views; their geometry is unchanged. Staff hatch60cm nominal, alcove headroom211.5cm and services require site verification."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A08",
      "description": "Upstairs 30 children +30 accompanying adults, plus 3 staff. The four activity-room areas printed on ERP total 96.27 m2, versus 129.405 m2 in the retained trace. Compact furniture/people rectangles individually stay within those printed areas; their shape/registration is a furnishing assumption, not surveyed walls. Geometry A03 remains unresolved."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A09",
      "description": "Thirty parent seats and room allocations14/4/4/8 are a busy occupancy proposal. Parent stature and breadth are independent; seated pose height is not scaled to standing stature. Child ages/statures and poses are illustrative. Corridors, toilets, exterior landing and service rooms contribute no visitor seats or spillover play."
    },
    {
      "id": "V1-A10",
      "description": "20/24/30-family comparisons change visible counts without resizing figures. The target of 60 visitors plus 3 upstairs staff is not certified daily comfort or a new opening authorisation. The signed 18 September 2026 record states 100 public +4 staff for the establishment and conditions remain applicable."
    }
  ],
